@startuml Maintenance-SD-StartupSync
autonumber
title Startup synchronisation of the read models (new, late or erased replica)
participant "maintenance-3\n(starting, empty database)" as M3
participant ": ReadModelSynchronizer\n(replica 3)" as Sync3
queue "aisafe.maintenance.events" as EX
participant "maintenance-1\n: ReadModelSynchronizer" as Sync1
participant "maintenance-1\n: MaintenanceStateRepublisher" as Rep1
participant "maintenance-2\n: MaintenanceStateRepublisher" as Rep2

M3 -> M3 : listeners start: queue maintenance-3.maintenance declared
M3 -> M3 : ReferenceTemplatesBootstrap, DemoDataBootstrap (own rows, own events)
M3 -> Sync3 : ApplicationReadyEvent
activate Sync3
Sync3 -> EX : republish the templates and records replica 3 OWNS (current version)
Sync3 -> EX : MaintenanceSyncRequested {requestedBy: maintenance-3}\n(key maintenance-sync.requested)
deactivate Sync3
EX -> Sync1 : sync request (replica 2 receives it too)
activate Sync1
Sync1 -> Rep1 : republishOwnedState("sync requested by maintenance-3")
Rep1 -> EX : MaintenanceTemplateCreated / MaintenanceRecordCreated|Completed\nfor every row replica 1 owns
deactivate Sync1
EX -> Rep2 : (same on replica 2)
Rep2 -> EX : events of every row replica 2 owns
EX -> M3 : all of them → projections → read models complete
note over M3, Rep2
  Replicas that already have a row apply an identical upsert (same version); older versions are ignored.
  The request uses another "aggregate" (maintenance-sync), so it does not match maintenance-record.*.
end note
@enduml
